WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:09.451
<v Audio Description>Visual scene one: Card one glows amber beside tall translucent wireframe forecast towers contrasted against a modest solid cyan earned-revenue bar.

2
00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:16.882
<v Presenter>First, headline trillion-dollar figures for AI coding are future guesses, not counts of money already earned.

3
00:00:17.222 --> 00:00:24.523
<v Audio Description>Visual scene two: Card two turns cyan while repeating rose token-meter rings spin endlessly above the forecast tower.

4
00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:30.877
<v Presenter>Second, almost every forecast assumes developers will pay a giant AI model by the word forever.

5
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:39.755
<v Audio Description>Visual scene three: Card three locks in emerald as saved, verified code blocks drop repeat-task bars down to the thin cyan electricity floor.

6
00:00:40.095 --> 00:00:47.630
<v Presenter>Third, saving and reusing working code drives repeated jobs toward electricity cost, making those forecasts too high.
